T069. Anchors from the corpus measured 2026-11-15 on this machine
(1,042 claude mains 1.29 GiB + 1,280 subagents 0.59 GiB; 2,495
codex rollouts 2.93 GiB; 74 pi files 2.1 MiB). Codex threads
(1,600 at scale 1) are derived from bytes because the generator
omits resumed pages; real threads ~511 over ~4.9 files each.
Query fixture answers the perf plan's open question "one million
events without a 3 GB input": text/8 + session-bytes/4 lands at
765-889 B mean records (JSON envelope is the floor), 969,004
events in 746.4 MiB vs ~3.5 GB at full record sizes.
Key constraints honored: Corpus.Compact with div=1 keeps legacy
bytes byte-identical (hashes captured pre-change and pinned);
fixgen imports only the parser packages because importing
internal/events cycles with events' in-package bench tests
(records->events is structurally 1:1, so raw parsers count
events exactly).
